# This is a sample canvas history test case file, the historygen.pl script will
# parse, check and generate C code for the actual test. Empty lines and lines
# starting with # are ignored. Other instructions are per-line. Ideally your
# test cases should have a *brief* comment on what they are about in the header
# and no ramble on the individual commands. Explaining sections is okay.
#
# The point of these is to test Drawpile's rollback netcode. Local commands are
# executed immediately and kept in a local fork of the canvas history until the
# command comes back from the remote. Remote commands from other users may come
# in along the way and are reconciled with the local fork. Conflicts cause the
# fork to be replayed. We only test realistic cases here: every local command
# will come back from the remote in order. This stuff is complicated enough
# without getting into cases that can never happen in normal operation.
# Particularly undos and redos have had many bugs in the past, since they have
# to roll back and forth commands while taking care not to restore a rolled-back
# local state or something.
#
# Each test case will be executed once for the "client", where local commands
# are sent immediately and then later received and reconciled from the remote,
# and once for the "server", where only the remote commands are handled. Then
# the results are compared, with the expectation that the canonical server side
# matches the local client side that went through the whole out-of-order
# rollback business. A mismatch always means that the client is wrong.
#
# Several commands have a local and a remote variant. The local variant means
# that the local user issued the command and is waiting for it to come back from
# the remote. A remote command means that another user issued the command. Some
# technical details: there is one layer, the local user is user 1, the remote
# user is user 2, the canvas background is always white. Each regular command
# will set an undo point.

# reset [width]x[height] [undo_limit]
# Reset command. Clears the history, sets the canvas size and undo limit.
# Minimum undo limit is 3, maximum is 255. This must be the first command in a
# test case and that is also the only place you can use it at currently. Unless
# you have a reason to do it differently, use these parameters.
reset 500x500 3

# [local|remote] resize [top],[right],[bottom],[left]
# Resizes the canvas in the given directions. Positive numbers expand the canvas
# in that direction, negative ones contract it.
local resize 0,100,200,0

# [local|remote] fill [x],[y] [width]x[height] [color]
# Fills a rectangular area of the canvas starting from the top-left coordinates
# and spanning for the given width and height with the given color. This command
# will conflict with any overlapping fills. For consistency, use red colors for
# local commands and blue colors for remote ones.
local fill 0,0 100x100 ff0000

# [local|remote] undo
# Undoes the effects of the last non-undone command. If the undo limit given in
# the last reset command is exceeded, this will do nothing. Note that the undo
# limit is shared between all users.
local undo

# [local|remote] redo
# Redoes the effects of the next undone command. If there is no undone command
# or the command has fallen beyond the undo limit, this will do nothing. Issuing
# a command that isn't undo or redo will cut off any undone commands.
local redo

# receive [n]
# Receives the next n not yet received local command(s) from the remote and
# reconciles them with the local state. Each local command must be received from
# the remote by the end of the test case. You also can't receive more commands
# than are left. The historygen.pl script will validate this.
receive 4

# check
# Checks whether the local and remote canvas look the same at this point. This
# happens automatically at the end of the test, but can be done in the middle as
# well. You can only use this command at points where all local commands have
# been received, since only then should the local and remote state be in sync.
check

# Some remote examples.
remote resize 20,20,20,20
remote fill 50,50 100x100 0000ff
remote undo
remote redo
